# GuardTalkOS — zumapro_stallion (zumapro / stallion) vendor_dlkm modules blocklist.
#
# T-PORT-EXCISION-MATRIX (P0): canonical blocklist for excision variant 'zumapro_stallion'.
# Derivation (mechanical, no invented entries):
#   upstream device/google/stallion-kernels/6.1/grapheneos/vendor_dlkm.modules.blocklist
#   + GuardTalk BT-excision addition 'blocklist nitrous' (T-BT-FULL FR-3, nitrous
#     BCM BT power/rfkill driver, present in vendor_dlkm.modules.load).
# Every upstream 'blocklist' line is preserved verbatim and in order.
# Devices mapped to this variant: see excision-variants.mk GT_DEVICE_VARIANT_*.
# In-force exemplars: vendor/guardtalk/device/{akita,komodo,rango}/vendor_dlkm.modules.blocklist.
#
# Wi-Fi two-phase load (upstream: blocklist in the bulk pass, then re-modprobe
# without -b in init.insmod.stallion.cfg) is preserved verbatim. WiFi is NOT broken.

blocklist aoc_unit_test_dev
blocklist mali_kutf
blocklist mali_kutf_clk_rate_trace_test_portal
blocklist sscoredump_sample_test.ko
blocklist sscoredump_test.ko
blocklist bcmdhd4383
blocklist cs40l26_i2c
blocklist pwm_exynos
blocklist rt4539_bl
blocklist sts4x_ambient_i2c
blocklist focal_touch.ko

# T-BT-FULL (FR-3): Bluetooth power/rfkill driver — BCM BT on UART.
blocklist nitrous
